matrix(LineageTable) -- extract a matrix of polynomials from values of a LineageTable after deleting null values
****************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)matrix,
  * Usage: 
        matrix LineageTable
  * Inputs:
      * H, an instance of the type *note LineageTable: LineageTable,, whose
        values are polynomials
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)matrix_lpList_rp, => ..., default value
        null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of non-null values of H

Description
===========

This simple function just returns the Gröbner basis computed with threaded
Gröbner basis function *note tgb: tgb, in the expected Macaulay2 format, so
that further computation are one step easier to set up.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                           |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : allowableThreads= 2;                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = reduce tgb( ideal "abc+c2,ab2-b3c+ac,b2")|
|                                                  |
|o3 = LineageTable{(((0, 1), 0), 0) => null}       |
|                  ((0, 1), 0) => null             |
|                                  2               |
|                  ((1, 2), 0) => c                |
|                  (0, 1) => null                  |
|                  (0, 2) => null                  |
|                  (1, 2) => a*c                   |
|                  0 => null                       |
|                  1 => null                       |
|                        2                         |
|                  2 => b                          |
|                                                  |
|o3 : LineageTable                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : matrix T                                     |
|                                                  |
|o4 = | b2 c2 ac |                                 |
|                                                  |
|             1      3                             |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

